Package: XenoPanel
Type: Package
Title: Configuration-Driven Analysis of Targeted Transcriptomic Panels
Version: 1.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person(given = "Spencer W.", family = "Frangou", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "spencer.frangou@utoledo.edu",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0008-1125-4053"))
Description: Analysis of targeted transcriptomic panel data (DriverMap and comparable
    targeted RNA assays) from xenografts and cell lines: estimation and masking of
    host-species cross-reactivity from a dilution series, filtering, TMM normalisation
    and differential expression with edgeR quasi-likelihood tests and TREAT, an exact
    decomposition of expression changes into heritable and environmental components
    over three states, and transcriptome diversity, network entropy (CCAT, SCENT),
    signature (singscore), PROGENy and CollecTRI activity scores. Inputs, modules,
    thresholds and contrasts are declared in a YAML configuration file.
